# Vendored artifacts ARE committed on purpose — registry/, parity/fixtures/ and
# wasm/ must be in the tree for the drift gate to have anything to check.

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

node_modules/
dist/
.expo/

target/
*.rs.bk
# ESP-IDF framework checkout, created by building a firmware crate in place.
.embuild/

# Local overrides of a reference body: copy config.toml to config.local.toml
# and edit that, so the committed body stays a clean template.
bodies/*/config.local.toml
bodies/*/*.db-wal
bodies/*/*.db-shm

# The two rules above never matched the files they were written for. The agent
# names its own SQLite databases after `[agent] name` with no extension, so a
# body called "trailwatch" produces `trailwatch`, `trailwatch-wal` and
# `trailwatch-shm` — not `*.db-wal`. bodies/trailwatch/ shipped all three (an
# empty scheduler database, 57 KB) from cce8731 on 2026-07-27 until 2026-08-02,
# ignored by a pattern that looked like it covered them. A current build writes
# to the OS data directory instead, so the bare database file cannot come back
# from a normal run; the sidecars are matched here anyway.
bodies/*/*-wal
bodies/*/*-shm

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
.env

# Commit messages written to a file and passed with `git commit -F`. Untracked
# and unignored is how scratch files get swept into a commit here — which
# happened upstream on 2026-08-01 with a `git add -A`.
_commitmsg.txt

# Scratch landing area. The Cowork device bridge cannot unlink files, so an
# agent working in this repo moves things here instead of deleting them. Twice
# now that has ended with scratch files committed by accident, because they show
# up as pending changes and get swept into a commit. Ignoring the directory
# removes the temptation rather than relying on nobody clicking it.
_to_delete/
